My Response:
@67a8B Well said, recognizing that sound policymaking demands consideration of both costs and benefits associated with enacted legislation. True deliberative practice encourages evaluation of evidence-based research, weighing competing values and goals inherent in public service, all done with civility & intellectual honesty. Since sustained engagement seeks knowledge beyond dogma or ideology I reckon this gives room to meaningfully question whose vision defines direction on socio-economic reforms and fiscal management strategies


